21
00:00:25,684 --> 00:00:27,104
That's not a pulse, that's a

22
00:00:27,114 --> 00:00:27,544
hum.

23
00:00:27,588 --> 00:00:28,128
But wait.

24
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,748
Why is his helmet steaming up?

25
00:00:29,792 --> 00:00:31,352
You see, all that food turns

26
00:00:31,362 --> 00:00:33,132
into heat, and Gus now puts

27
00:00:33,142 --> 00:00:34,422
out as much as four space

28
00:00:34,432 --> 00:00:35,002
heaters.

29
00:00:35,046 --> 00:00:36,606
Ever notice a french fry goes

30
00:00:36,616 --> 00:00:38,436
cold in minutes, but a baked

31
00:00:38,446 --> 00:00:40,116
potato stays hot for half an

32
00:00:40,126 --> 00:00:40,466
hour?

33
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:42,170
Small things have more skin for

34
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:42,980
their size.

35
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,710
Pound for pound, the bird has

36
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,570
twenty times more than Gus, so

37
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,040
